AUDIO: 'Hey, man. How you holding up? Oh, I\'m all right, I guess. I heard about what happened. Yeah. Well, for what it\'s worth, I thought the Retroid Pocket Nova was a really swell handheld. Um'

[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'what? Your Retroid Pocket Nova. It\'s broken, right? Uh no. No, my Nova\'s good. It\'s right here. I love this thing. Wait, then why are you sad? Because the person watching this video'

[00:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'isn\'t subscribed to Tech Beep. What video? This video. I\'m filming a video right now. Wait, what? Yeah. See the camera right there? Dude, you got to tell me if you\'re filming a video.'

[00:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Sorry. Do you want to start over? Yes. Okay. Hey, man. [music] How you holding up? Oh, I\'m all right, I guess. &gt;&gt; [music]'

[00:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; If you\'ve been hearing a lot about the Retroid Pocket Nova, you\'re not [music] alone. The Nova has taken the world by storm. Everyone\'s talking about it. It\'s literally changed the course of human existence, probably. [music] Our'

[01:04] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'children\'s children\'s children will look back on this as the dawn of a glorious Retroid Nova-based era. Or they\'ll ask, "What\'s a Retroid Nova?" and I\'ll be dead, so I can\'t tell them. But that got me thinking. Why? Why does everyone love'

[01:17] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'this thing so much? I mean, it\'s a retro handheld, and we love retro handhelds, but there\'s lots of retro handhelds that are retro handhelds. The Nova feels different. The reviews are all glowing,'

[01:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'tons of YouTube videos, Reddit loves it, Twitter stuff, too, maybe. There\'s just so much love for this stupid little thing. So, what makes it special? Is it the screen, the shape and size, the controls, the power, or just the fact'

[01:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that it\'s called Nova, which is a very powerful space word? I think the real answer is some of that stuff, but also some other stuff that I didn\'t say just now, because that\'s what the whole video will be about. The Nova is a champ, and'

[01:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'we love it for some really good reasons. So, today I\'m going to go through those reasons and because this is YouTube, I made it a top 10 list. That\'s just how it\'s done with us YouTube video making people. We love [music] lists. We also'

[02:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'love asking you to subscribe, but I\'m not going to do that because you\'re smart and cool and you probably subscribed already. That\'s what smart and cool people do after all. Anyways, without further mucking about, as we say in Canada, let\'s get this Nova love fest'

[02:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'started, shall [music] we? The most obvious thing that sets the Nova apart from literally every other handheld is the screen. There are no other handhelds with a big 4x3 high refresh rate OLED'

[02:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'screen. Hopefully that changes, but for now, the Nova is the only one. The one and only. The onlyest one of the ones that are owned. [music] First of all, 4x3. That\'s the retro game ratio.'

[02:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'GameCube, PS2, Super Nintendo, Genesis, and most of the other old stuff was 4x3. So, if you prioritize retro games, you probably want a screen that actually fits them instead of having ugly black'

[02:58] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'bars beside everything. And because it\'s OLED, games look amazing. Super bright with rich saturated colors and pure dark inky blacks. Everyone loves OLED for good reasons. It makes our eyeballs happy. It\'s also 120 hertz, so Android'

[03:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and menus are silky smooth and you can use black frame insertion for retro games if you\'re into that. And my favorite, older PC games can run at their full silky smooth native frame rates. And 4.5 inches is a great size.'

[03:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Nice and big so we can actually see our games with our aging eyes. There are 4x3 handhelds and OLED handhelds and high refresh rate handhelds, but the Nova combines all three and that\'s probably'

[03:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the best thing about it, apart from the other things on this list that you might think are better. Another thing that makes the Nova especially good for retro games is the D-pad centric layout. The D-pad is up top and the analog stick is'

[03:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'underneath, which is the correct arrangement, according to me, the grand retro handheld overlord that I am. Obviously, there\'s no layout that\'s perfect for everything. Modern stuff likes sticks better, but for retro stuff'

[04:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'like NES and Super Nintendo and Genesis and Gameboy, that stuff was made for D-pads. And I want that D-pad right where my thumb naturally lands. Plenty of powerful retro handhelds put the analog stick up top, especially devices'

[04:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'designed for GameCube and PS2. I understand why, but personally, I still spend more time playing older 2D games, so I\'d rather prioritize the D-pad. It helps that the D-pad itself is really'

[04:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'good, too. It\'s that classic Retroid D-pad. Clicky, but not loud, precise, nice diagonals, great for platformers and fighting games and everything, really. And the sticks are still comfortable for when I need them, so I I'

[04:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'don\'t feel like I\'m sacrificing much. It\'s a small design choice, but on a handheld that\'s primarily meant for playing old video games, putting the old video game button in the good spot seems like a easy choice. Most high-end'

[04:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'handhelds can play a ton of stuff, but the Nova is one of them, [music] and it can play that stuff, too. That doesn\'t make it uh special compared to the Retroid Pocket 6 or the Odin 2 Portal or the Ayn Thor. Same chip, same stuff. But'

[05:04] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'on the Nova, having all that power is what makes the other special stuff uh come together. You get the 4x3 screen, the retro first controls and vibes, and enough power to play basically the'

[05:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'entire history of retro games. Obviously, you got like Nintendo and Super Nintendo and Genesis and Gameboy and Gameboy Advance and arcade stuff, that all runs on a potato now, probably literally. But you also got N64 and Dreamcast and Sega Saturn and PSP and'

[05:30] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'GameCube and PS2 and Wii and 3DS and Switch, and most of that stuff is 4x3, so it fills this beautiful screen instead of floating in a rectangle surrounded by the dark abyss. Even'

[05:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'widescreen stuff like PSP still looks plenty big and plays great. Again, none of this is unique. The Nova isn\'t special because it plays this stuff. It\'s special because it plays all this stuff while being the Nova.'

[05:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'That sounded more profound in my head. The Nova also has a bunch of fancy modern quality of life stuff you don\'t necessarily expect from a little retro game rectangle. It has Wi-Fi 7 and'

[06:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Bluetooth 5.3, so you get fast modern wireless protocols for like headphones and controllers, streaming, and all the other invisible radio waves we\'ve decided to surround ourselves with. It also has 27 watt fast charging, so that'

[06:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'when you do need to fill the battery back up, it doesn\'t take forever. And it supports charging separation, which lets you bypass the battery entirely and power the Nova directly when it\'s plugged in if you like playing docked'

[06:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'mode. And speaking of docked mode, this is a big one for me. The Nova lets you connect this to an external monitor. TechWeave, you said external monitor. Y- Yeah. We have a sponsor segment and though that Oh, right. Right. So, let\'s'

[06:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'do it do that now. Yeah. Yeah, that probably makes sense. Noise. Oh, man. I have so much games to play, but I have so little screen. Just think'

[06:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'about how much more gaming would be gamed if I had a nice big external monitor. I would order that one everyone\'s always talking about, the Arzopa Z3FC. I\'d open it up and be blown away at how thin and'

[07:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'light and premium it felt. Not to mention how easy and effortless it is to get a big screen gaming experience without needing to buy a whole big setup. And I could finally be happy despite my dark past. Then I\'d probably'

[07:23] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'head to my favorite cafe to play some video games in public, so everyone would be super jealous at my super big 16.1-in display, silky smooth high refresh rate, and perfectly crispy 1440p resolution'

[07:35] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'for that competitive advantage. Maybe I\'d even use it to get a bit of work done. Plug in my laptop for that flawless dual screen workflow that having a second monitor gives you. I could even take it fun places like the'

[07:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'park to elevate my senses while I watch a movie to forget my troubled past that haunts me every waking minute. Oh, well. I guess I\'m just stuck gaming on this one tiny little screen.'

[08:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Unless [music] you too can check out the Ares Zopa Z3 FC using the link in the description below. And thanks Ares Zopa for sponsoring the video.'

[08:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'And on that topic, yeah, the the Nova can totally do video out. Plug the Nova into a compatible dongle or dock, hook it up to your TV or monitor, and it can output all the way up to 4K 60 Hz. So, this tiny handheld can basically become'

[08:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'a little retro console. Plug it into the TV, connect a Bluetooth controller, and sit back on the couch and play your stuff on the big screen like a cool guy. And you can even switch the display mode so you can do full wide screen stuff'

[08:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'while docked. If you like things that do multiple things, the Nova has you covered. It\'s a handheld and a console and a butt scratcher. The Nova uses the Snapdragon 8 Gen 2'

[08:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'chip, more or less, which means we got plenty of power to play a ton of stuff. But what I think most people get excited about with the Nova is how GameCube and PS2 stop feeling like something you have to worry about. On cheaper handhelds,'

[09:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'these systems can turn into a whole project. Which emulator should I use? Which rendering engine and GPU drivers? What resolution? What about underclocking and performance hacks? Why is Sly Cooper running like he\'s'

[09:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'underwater? On the Nova, for the vast majority of PS2 and GameCube games, you just set them to 2x resolution and play. That\'s it. They look crisp, they run great, and you don\'t have to spend 20 minutes fiddling with the settings'

[09:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'before remembering that you\'re supposed to be having fun. Obviously, emulation is emulation, so there will always be weird games and emulator specific issues, but the Nova has enough raw horsepower that the device generally isn\'t the problem. And that\'s the kind'

[09:46] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'of power I actually care about in a retro handheld. Not benchmark numbers, not theoretical maximum gig of flops per compute core. I just want to click GameCube and get GameCube. No monkey business. Unless I\'m playing as Donkey'

[10:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Kong in Mario Kart. Then, yes, monkey business. All right, ergonomics. [music] A lot of powerful handhelds have permanent ergonomic humps, which can be comfortable, but also make them thicker and harder to shove into a pocket. The'

[10:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Nova is just flat, slimmer, lighter, easier to carry, no big old booty sticking out the back. I can\'t demonstrate pocketability because my pocket test guy is currently not here. We haven\'t heard from him in a few'

[10:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'weeks, and well, if anyone in northern Ontario sees a guy with temp on his shirt wandering around in the woods, please let us know. We\'re all very worried about him. Anyways, if you want more curves to hold'

[10:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'on to, Retroid makes a swappable ergonomic back plate with proper grips. It comes with pre-orders, or you can just buy it separately for like five bucks. I got one, and I did try it, and I do like it. It\'s comfy, especially for dual stick games, but I went back to'

[10:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'flat. I\'m a flat guy. It keeps the Nova slimmer, but I also like that it doesn\'t tell my hands where to go. I can shift my grip around wherever I want. But what\'s great is that the Nova gives you the choice, curvy or flat. Everybody gets the butt they deserve. And while'

[11:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'we\'re talking about how the Nova feels, the controls are just really good across the board. You got 3D Hall Effect analog sticks and Hall Effect triggers. So, they\'re accurate, smooth, and you don\'t have to worry about stick drift'

[11:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'developing over time. The face buttons are great, too. They use a nice quiet membrane with enough travel to feel satisfying without being overly mushy. I\'ve played a lot of games on this thing, and everything just feels right,'

[11:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'which is about the highest compliment that I can give controls. I don\'t think about them. And up top, you got properly stacked shoulder buttons instead of inline ones. R1 and R2 actually sit on top of each other like they do on a'

[11:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'normal modern controller. And you get rebindable function buttons up there, too, which can be customized but pretty much however you like. None of these things are revolutionary on their own. Sticks, buttons, stacked shoulders, but'

[11:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'so many handhelds screw something [music] up. The Nova didn\'t. There\'s no part of this that feels like they\'re trying to cut corners. It passes the extremely rigorous does Tech Tuber complain about it test. And I got to say that the Nova really nails the battery'

[12:09] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'life. It has a 5,000 mA hour battery, and that efficient chip in there makes it go a long way. With heavier GameCube or PS2, you can get around 5 to 6 hours, which is plenty. But later stuff like'

[12:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Super Nintendo or Gameboy Advance or game streaming can push well beyond 20 hours. I\'ve been taking it even further with an app called Cluster Tune, which lets you lower the CPU and GPU clocks when you don\'t need all that power. Dial'

[12:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'things back, and you can squeeze even more life out of it. Even PC games through Game Native can last surprisingly long. Older games can run great at around 30 FPS without needing anywhere near the Nova\'s full power. And'

[12:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you get Android sleep mode. Leave a game running, sleep the Nova, come back hours or days later, and you\'re back in your game in like 2 seconds. Let\'s see any PC handheld do that.'

[12:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'They can\'t. That\'s why I said it. One thing I didn\'t expect that really surprised me is that the Nova doesn\'t really feel like a premium piece of technology. And I mean that as like a good thing. It\'s plastic. Nice plastic,'

[13:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'but plastic. It\'s matte, lightweight, and it comes in colors like ice blue and watermelon and 16-bit with these lovely retro DMG style buttons. It feels more like a Gameboy than a smartphone. It\'s'

[13:22] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'approachable. And importantly, it\'s grabbable. I don\'t feel like I need to gently retrieve it from its velvet pedestal with freshly washed hands. It\'s just sitting there, I grab it, I play it, and I think that that vibe fits'

[13:35] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'retro games perfectly. These games weren\'t originally played on giant glass screens and brushed aluminum rectangles. They were played on chunky plastic toys that got thrown into backpacks. It\'s hard to describe, but the Nova captures'

[13:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'a little bit of that feeling of an actual retro handheld. And combined with everything else, the 4x3 OLED, the D-pad up top, the power to play basically everything, it feels like a complete package. Retro games feel like they'

[14:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'belong on the Nova. It\'s fancy technology disguised as a toy, which is great for a child pretending to be an adult, like me. And now, the final reason that the Retroid Pocket Nova is great is'

[14:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'I don\'t know. I can\'t answer that because number 10 is your reason. Because there\'s always something about the stuff that we love that doesn\'t fit on a spec sheet or a top 10 list. Maybe your Nova lives in your pocket and comes'

[14:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'out whenever you\'re stuck waiting somewhere. Maybe you just had a kid, and while your little homie naps on you and drools through your shirt, you squeeze in a few rounds of Mario Kart. Maybe you\'ve always dreamed of having a portable GameCube, and now you do. Maybe'

[14:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you played one specific game during a weird time in your life, and now this little plastic rectangle is permanently connected to that memory. That kind of stuff is what I\'m talking about here. That that\'s your thing. The Nova feels like that to me, and I think that\'s kind'

[14:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'of kind of one of the unexplained reasons why everyone seems to be gushing about this. It\'s special in a way that\'s that different for everyone. So, number 10, I don\'t know. You tell me. And that\'s it. That\'s my list. It turns out'

[15:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that people love the Nova because it\'s really good in lots of ways. I know, incredible investigative journalism happening here today. All the things I said is just all the all the things that come together into one extremely lovable'

[15:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'rectangle. Is it perfect? Nope. Is it going to change the course of human civilization like I predicted at the beginning? Yes. Yes, it will. So, enjoy this brief moment in history before the'

[15:30] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Retroid Pocket Nova 2 comes out and we all throw these directly into the ocean. Anyways, that\'ll do it for me for today. I\'m TechBoot. Thanks for watching. Bye-bye. &gt;&gt; [music]'
